# PRD.md — Ozzie Quran App (MVP)

## 0) What this is
Ozzie is a kid-focused Quran learning app that teaches recitation through a structured loop:
Surah → Ayah learning → Recitation attempts + feedback → Mini quizzes → Final exam → Rewards + progress tracking.

The project MUST be “real” end-to-end:
- real auth
- real database writes
- real rules enforcement
- real audio uploads
- real scoring responses (even if scoring is v1 simple)

## 1) Users & roles
### Parent (account owner)
- Sign up/sign in via email (Supabase Auth)
- Set/enter parental gate PIN
- Create/manage multiple child profiles
- View child progress dashboards
- Configure child settings (limits, notifications, etc.)

### Child (app user)
- Enters child mode after parental gate + child selection
- Uses learning loop to master ayahs and surahs
- Receives rewards (Hasanat, badges) and sees progress

## 2) MVP goals
- A parent can create/select a child and start a learning session.
- A child can complete the ayah learning loop with real audio submission and a scored result.
- The app enforces learning constraints (attempt budgets, passes required, quiz gating).
- Mini quizzes and final exam are triggered in the agreed order.
- Progress dashboards show streak/time/score and attempt logs.

## 3) Non-goals (MVP)
- Perfect tajweed/makhraj grading (can be v2/v3)
- Fully polished animations/mascot interactions
- Deep analytics beyond core dashboards
- A clean “production-grade” Figma file (we use it as reference, not source of truth)

## 4) Core learning model (3 layers)
This is the single most important conceptual alignment.

### A) Attempt layer (micro: per submission)
Definition: An attempt is one recorded recitation submission for a specific ayah.

Hard constraints (server-enforced):
- Max attempts per day: 6
- Real-time detailed feedback attempts per day: 3
- Intervention after consecutive failures: after 2 consecutive fails, force a “Learn” intervention before allowing further tries (replay audio / show hints / re-read).

Optional experiment:
- Blur verse text on 3rd attempt (A/B), to compare “blurry vs clear”.

### B) Ayah mastery layer (meso: mastery requirement)
Definition: An ayah is “mastered” only after PASS is achieved at least 3 times (cumulative).

Rules:
- passesRequired = 3
- Passing score threshold is configurable (benchmark-dependent).
- Pass count persists across days.
- Daily attempt count resets daily.

UX implication:
- After first pass, show “2 more tries” (meaning 2 more passing attempts required).

### C) Surah progression layer (macro: Learn → Mini Quiz → Final Exam)
Curriculum is divided into 3 parts:
1) Learn (ayah mastery loop)
2) Mini Quiz (“pop quiz”)
3) Final Exam

Agreed quiz order:
- After 2 verses → Mini Quiz #1
- Total 2 mini quizzes → then Final Exam

Suggested mapping (example for 7-ayah surah):
- Learn 1–2 → Mini Quiz 1 (covers 1–2)
- Learn 3–4 → Mini Quiz 2 (covers 3–4)
- Learn 5–7 → Final Exam (covers 1–7)

## 5) Core app flows (MVP)
### Parent onboarding flow
1) Splash / Onboarding (optional)
2) Sign up / Sign in (email)
3) Verify email success
4) Set PIN (first time) / Enter PIN (returning)
5) Select child (if >1 child)
6) Add child (if none)

Edge case:
- If parent has exactly one child, skip child selection after PIN.

### Child learning flow (golden path)
1) Child Home (journey/path UI)
2) Select Surah → Surah Overview
3) Start Ayah flow
4) Learn step (illustration + verse/meaning + listen)
5) Recite step (record → review → submit)
6) Feedback (success/fail; may show attempts remaining)
7) Continue loop until mastery/gate:
   - Mini Quiz after ayah 2 and 4
   - Final Exam after mini quiz 2 and remaining ayahs learned

### Progress & dashboards
Child:
- Streak calendar
- Recite time / sessions
- Score trends + activity log

Parent:
- Per-child summary + controls + settings

## 6) UI/UX directives (must-follow)
- Illustrations must be large and comfortably viewable; reserve a stable illustration slot on learning screens.
- Do NOT show a heavy “stats top bar” at early quiz stages (keep UI focused).
- Pathway visualization does not need galaxy everywhere; can be simplified (circles / creative abstractions).
- Keep quiz order exactly as agreed (no rearranging).
- The design files are messy; treat the design system reference + screenshots as guidance, not a generator.

## 7) Definition of done (MVP)
- Supabase auth working (real)
- Parent PIN gate + child CRUD working (real)
- Surah/Ayah content displayed (real source; cached OK)
- Audio recording, upload, scoring, and attempt logging working (real)
- Server-enforced rules:
  - daily attempts cap (6)
  - realtime feedback cap (3)
  - passes required (3)
  - mini quiz gating order
- Progress dashboards populated from real DB data

